BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   - Summing over all volume elements in V, the internal boundary fluxes between adjoining) Tj
T*
(   interior cells cancel identically in pairs because outward normals on adjoining shared faces) Tj
T*
(   point in opposite directions.) Tj
T*
(   - Only the flux across the external bounding surface S survives:) Tj
T*
(   Closed_Integral_S \(F dot dS\) = Integral_V \(Del dot F\) dV. \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Application to Maxwell's First Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Gauss's Law in integral form: Closed_Integral_S \(D dot dS\) = Q_enclosed = Integral_V \(rho_v\)) Tj
T*
(   dV.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying divergence theorem: Integral_V \(Del dot D\) dV = Integral_V \(rho_v\) dV.) Tj
T*
(   - Since this holds for an arbitrary volume V: Del dot D = rho_v \(Differential Form\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove Stokes's Theorem. Demonstrate how it connects Faraday's Law in integral and differential forms.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of Stokes's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   The circulation of a vector field F around a closed contour C is equal to the surface integral) Tj
T*
(   of the curl of F over any open surface S bounded by C:) Tj
T*
(   Closed_Integral_C \(F dot dl\) = Integral_S \( \(Del x F\) dot dS \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Proof Outline:) Tj
T*
(   - Partition the open surface S into microscopic planar rectangular elements of dimensions dx) Tj
T*
(   and dy.) Tj
T*
(   - Consider an elementary loop in the xy-plane with vertices at \(x,y\), \(x+dx,y\), \(x+dx,y+dy\),) Tj
T*
(   \(x,y+dy\).) Tj
T*
(   - The line integral around this counter-clockwise elementary loop is:) Tj
T*
(   dGamma = F_x\(x,y\)*dx + F_y\(x+dx,y\)*dy - F_x\(x,y+dy\)*dx - F_y\(x,y\)*dy) Tj
T*
(   = - [ \(dF_x/dy\)*dy ] * dx + [ \(dF_y/dx\)*dx ] * dy) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(dF_y/dx\) - \(dF_x/dy\) ] * dx * dy = \(Del x F\)_z * dS_z.) Tj
T*
(   - Extending this to all three spatial components in arbitrary orientation:) Tj
T*
(   dGamma = \(Del x F\) dot dS.) Tj
T*
(   - Summing over all surface elements, line integrals along shared interior edges cancel because) Tj
T*
(   they are traversed in opposite directions.) Tj
T*
(   - Only the line integral along the external boundary curve C remains:) Tj
T*
(   Closed_Integral_C \(F dot dl\) = Integral_S \( \(Del x F\) dot dS \). \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Connection to Faraday's Law:) Tj
T*
(   - Integral form: emf = Closed_Integral_C \(E dot dl\) = - d\(Phi_B\) / dt = - d/dt Integral_S \(B) Tj
T*
(   dot dS\).) Tj
T*
(   - Applying Stokes's Theorem to the left-hand side:) Tj
T*
(   Integral_S \( \(Del x E\) dot dS \) = - Integral_S \( \(dB/dt\) dot dS \).) Tj
T*
(   - For an arbitrary surface S: Del x E = - dB / dt \(Differential Form\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
