(   must flow outward across the surface S as an electric current.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   - Total enclosed charge: Q\(t\) = Integral_V rho\(x,y,z,t\) dV, where rho is volume charge density) Tj
T*
(   \(C/m^3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Net outward current leaving through bounding surface S:) Tj
T*
(   I_out = Closed_Integral_S \(J dot dS\), where J is current density vector \(A/m^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - By charge conservation: I_out = - dQ / dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting expressions:) Tj
T*
(   Closed_Integral_S \(J dot dS\) = - d/dt Integral_V rho dV = - Integral_V \(d\(rho\)/dt\) dV.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Application of Gauss's Divergence Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   - Transform the surface integral into a volume integral:) Tj
T*
(   Integral_V \(Del dot J\) dV = - Integral_V \(d\(rho\)/dt\) dV.) Tj
T*
(   - Rearranging: Integral_V [ Del dot J + d\(rho\)/dt ] dV = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since the volume V is completely arbitrary, the integrand must vanish identically everywhere:) Tj
T*
(   Del dot J = - d\(rho\) / dt \(Differential Equation of Continuity\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Physical Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - In steady-state DC systems: d\(rho\)/dt = 0, which yields Del dot J = 0 \(Kirchhoff's Current) Tj
T*
(   Law at a point\).) Tj
T*
(   - In AC and transient electrodynamic systems: d\(rho\)/dt != 0, proving that diverging conduction) Tj
T*
(   current implies a local depletion of charge.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
