(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the parallel-plate capacitor paradox during charging, and prove mathematically that conduction current in the leads equals displacement current between the plates.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Capacitor Paradox:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider a circular parallel-plate capacitor of plate area A and separation d being charged) Tj
T*
(   by current i_c\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Choose a closed loop C encircling the wire feeding the positive plate.) Tj
T*
(   - Let S1 be a flat surface bounded by C that passes through the connecting wire.) Tj
T*
(   - Let S2 be a bag-shaped surface bounded by the same loop C that balloons out between the) Tj
T*
(   capacitor plates without touching either plate.) Tj
T*
(   - By original Ampere's law: Closed_Integral_C \(B dot dl\) = mu_0 * I_through_S.) Tj
T*
(   - For surface S1: I_through_S1 = i_c \(conduction current\). Hence B != 0.) Tj
T*
(   - For surface S2: No conduction current flows through the vacuum/dielectric between plates \(i_c) Tj
T*
(   = 0\). Thus Ampere's law predicts B = 0!) Tj
T*
(   - A single physical loop C cannot have two different magnetic fields simultaneously. This was) Tj
T*
(   the famous capacitor paradox.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Resolution via Displacement Current:) Tj
T*
(   - Let charge on plates at instant t be q\(t\). Surface charge density: sigma = q\(t\) / A.) Tj
T*
(   - Electric field between plates: E\(t\) = sigma / epsilon = q\(t\) / \(epsilon * A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Electric flux through surface S2: Phi_E = E\(t\) * A = q\(t\) / epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   - The displacement current passing through surface S2 is:) Tj
T*
(   i_d = Integral_S2 \(J_d dot dS\) = Integral_S2 [ epsilon * \(dE/dt\) ] dS = epsilon * \(dPhi_E /) Tj
T*
(   dt\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting Phi_E: i_d = epsilon * d/dt [ q\(t\) / epsilon ] = dq\(t\) / dt.) Tj
T*
(   - By definition of conduction current: i_c = dq\(t\) / dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: i_d = i_c at every instant of time!) Tj
T*
(   - The total current \(i_c + i_d\) is perfectly continuous across the circuit, completely) Tj
T*
(   resolving the paradox.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
