(   [Problem Statement]: State all four Maxwell's equations in both differential and integral forms for general media, and explain the physical law underlying each equation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Maxwell's Equation I \(Gauss's Law for Electrostatics\):) Tj
T*
(   - Differential Form: Del dot D = rho_free) Tj
T*
(   - Integral Form: Closed_Integral_S \(D dot dS\) = Q_free,enclosed = Integral_V rho_free dV) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Basis: Coulomb's Inverse Square Law. Net electric displacement flux through any) Tj
T*
(   closed surface is proportional to total free electric charge enclosed. Electric field lines) Tj
T*
(   originate on positive charges and terminate on negative charges.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Maxwell's Equation II \(Gauss's Law for Magnetism\):) Tj
T*
(   - Differential Form: Del dot B = 0) Tj
T*
(   - Integral Form: Closed_Integral_S \(B dot dS\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Basis: Absence of isolated magnetic charges \(magnetic monopoles\). Magnetic flux) Tj
T*
(   lines are continuous closed loops; every magnetic north pole is paired with an equal south) Tj
T*
(   pole.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Maxwell's Equation III \(Faraday's Law of Induction\):) Tj
T*
