BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the electromagnetic wave equation for electric field E in a linear, isotropic, homogeneous, and charge-free dielectric medium.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Starting Maxwell's Equations in Source-Free Dielectric \(rho = 0, J = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   - \(1\) Del dot E = 0) Tj
T*
(   - \(2\) Del dot H = 0) Tj
T*
(   - \(3\) Del x E = - mu * \(dH / dt\)) Tj
T*
(   - \(4\) Del x H = epsilon * \(dE / dt\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Take the curl of Faraday's Law \(Eq 3\):) Tj
T*
(   Del x \(Del x E\) = Del x [ - mu * \(dH / dt\) ] = - mu * d/dt \(Del x H\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute Ampere-Maxwell's Law \(Eq 4\) into the right-hand side:) Tj
T*
(   Del x \(Del x E\) = - mu * d/dt [ epsilon * \(dE / dt\) ] = - mu * epsilon * \(d^2E / dt^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Apply the standard vector calculus Laplacian identity to the left-hand side:) Tj
T*
(   Del x \(Del x E\) = Del \(Del dot E\) - Del^2\(E\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since the medium is charge-free \(rho = 0\), Gauss's Law gives Del dot E = 0. Therefore Del\(Del) Tj
T*
(   dot E\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - The identity reduces to: - Del^2\(E\) = - mu * epsilon * \(d^2E / dt^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Simplifying signs yields the classic 3D vector wave equation:) Tj
T*
(   Del^2\(E\) = mu * epsilon * \(d^2E / dt^2\) [Helmholtz Wave Equation].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Comparison with General 3D Classical Wave Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Standard wave equation: Del^2\(psi\) = \(1 / v^2\) * \(d^2psi / dt^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Comparing coefficients: 1 / v^2 = mu * epsilon => v = 1 / sqrt\(mu * epsilon\).) Tj
T*
(   - In free vacuum: v = c = 1 / sqrt\(mu_0 * epsilon_0\) ~= 3.0 x 10^8 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the electromagnetic wave equation for magnetic field H in a charge-free dielectric, and compare its phase velocity with that of the electric field.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Maxwell's Curl Equations in Non-Conducting Medium \(J = 0, rho = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   - Del x E = - mu * \(dH / dt\)) Tj
T*
(   - Del x H = epsilon * \(dE / dt\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation for Magnetic Field H:) Tj
T*
(   - Take the curl of the Ampere-Maxwell Law:) Tj
T*
(   Del x \(Del x H\) = Del x [ epsilon * \(dE / dt\) ] = epsilon * d/dt \(Del x E\).) Tj
T*
