() Tj
T*
(   3. Evaluating the Ratio and Intrinsic Impedance:) Tj
T*
(   - Note that wave number k = omega / c = omega * sqrt\(mu_0 * epsilon_0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Amplitude of H_y: H_0 = \(k * E_0\) / \(mu_0 * omega\) = [ omega*sqrt\(mu_0*epsilon_0\) * E_0 ] /) Tj
T*
(   \(mu_0*omega\) = sqrt\(epsilon_0 / mu_0\) * E_0.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, the ratio of electric to magnetic field amplitude is defined as the intrinsic wave) Tj
T*
(   impedance eta_0:) Tj
T*
(   eta_0 = E_0 / H_0 = sqrt\(mu_0 / epsilon_0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Numerical Calculation in Free Space:) Tj
T*
(   mu_0 = 4*pi * 10^-7 H/m, epsilon_0 = 8.8541878 x 10^-12 F/m.) Tj
T*
(   eta_0 = sqrt\( \(4*pi * 10^-7\) / \(8.8541878 x 10^-12\) \) = 376.73 Ohms \(~ 120*pi Ohms ~ 377 Ohms\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 12:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and derive Poynting's Theorem from Maxwell's equations. Provide the physical interpretation of each term in the resulting equation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of Poynting's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Poynting's theorem represents the law of conservation of electromagnetic energy for) Tj
T*
(   electrodynamic systems. It states that the rate of energy flowing out of a closed volume equals) Tj
T*
(   the rate of decrease of stored electromagnetic energy minus the work done on charges \(ohmic) Tj
T*
(   losses\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Maxwell's curl equations:) Tj
T*
(   \(1\) Del x E = - dB / dt = - mu * \(dH / dt\)) Tj
T*
(   \(2\) Del x H = J + dD / dt = J + epsilon * \(dE / dt\)) Tj
T*
(   - Consider the vector identity for the divergence of a cross product:) Tj
T*
(   Del dot \(E x H\) = H dot \(Del x E\) - E dot \(Del x H\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute curl expressions \(1\) and \(2\) into the identity:) Tj
T*
(   Del dot \(E x H\) = H dot [ - mu * \(dH/dt\) ] - E dot [ J + epsilon * \(dE/dt\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = - mu * H dot \(dH/dt\) - epsilon * E dot \(dE/dt\) - J dot E.) Tj
T*
(   - Notice that: mu * H dot \(dH/dt\) = d/dt [ 0.5 * mu * H^2 ], and epsilon * E dot \(dE/dt\) = d/dt) Tj
T*
(   [ 0.5 * epsilon * E^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   Del dot \(E x H\) = - d/dt [ 0.5*epsilon*E^2 + 0.5*mu*H^2 ] - J dot E.) Tj
T*
(   - Defining the Poynting vector S = E x H and integrating over volume V:) Tj
T*
(   Integral_V [ Del dot S ] dV = - d/dt Integral_V [ 0.5*epsilon*E^2 + 0.5*mu*H^2 ] dV -) Tj
T*
(   Integral_V \(J dot E\) dV.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
