BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Define skin depth \(depth of penetration\). Derive its formula for a good conductor and explain its engineering consequences in structural grounding and EM shielding.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Skin Depth:) Tj
T*
(   - When an electromagnetic wave penetrates a conducting medium, its electric field amplitude) Tj
T*
(   decays exponentially with distance z:) Tj
T*
(   E\(z\) = E_0 * exp\(-alpha * z\) * cos\(omega*t - beta*z\).) Tj
T*
(   - Skin depth \(delta\) is defined as the depth beneath the conductor surface at which wave) Tj
T*
(   amplitude decays to 1/e \(~36.8%\) of its surface value:) Tj
T*
(   exp\(-alpha * delta\) = exp\(-1\) => delta = 1 / alpha.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation for a Good Conductor \(sigma >> omega * epsilon\):) Tj
T*
(   - In a good conductor, the conduction current dominates displacement current: sigma / \(omega *) Tj
T*
(   epsilon\) >> 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Complex propagation constant:) Tj
T*
(   gamma = sqrt\( j * omega * mu * sigma \) = sqrt\( omega * mu * sigma \) * sqrt\(j\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since sqrt\(j\) = exp\(j*pi/4\) = \(1 + j\) / sqrt\(2\):) Tj
T*
(   gamma = sqrt\( omega * mu * sigma / 2 \) * \(1 + j\) = alpha + j * beta.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: alpha = beta = sqrt\( omega * mu * sigma / 2 \) = sqrt\( pi * f * mu * sigma \).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting into skin depth formula:) Tj
T*
(   delta = 1 / alpha = sqrt\( 2 / \(omega * mu * sigma\) \) = 1 / sqrt\( pi * f * mu * sigma \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Engineering Implications:) Tj
T*
(   - Structural Grounding and Rebar: At 50/60 Hz, skin depth in steel rebar is a few millimeters.) Tj
T*
(   For lightning surges \(high frequency components up to tens of MHz\), current concentrates) Tj
T*
(   entirely in a microscopic outer layer, drastically increasing effective AC resistance.) Tj
T*
(   - EM Shielding of Control Rooms: High-conductivity copper or aluminum enclosures must exceed) Tj
T*
(   several skin depths in thickness \(t > 5*delta\) to attenuate ambient electromagnetic) Tj
T*
(   interference by over 40 dB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

