BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the working principles of Ground Penetrating Radar \(GPR\) in civil engineering. How do permittivity and conductivity govern radar depth and resolution?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Working Principle of GPR:) Tj
T*
(   - Ground Penetrating Radar \(GPR\) is a non-destructive geophysical and civil structural) Tj
T*
(   diagnostic tool.) Tj
T*
(   - A transmitting antenna emits nanosecond-duration pulses of high-frequency electromagnetic) Tj
T*
(   waves \(typically 100 MHz to 2.5 GHz\) into a civil structure \(e.g., concrete bridge deck,) Tj
T*
(   highway pavement, retaining wall\).) Tj
T*
(   - As the wave travels downward, differences in electromagnetic properties at subsurface) Tj
T*
(   interfaces \(rebar, voids, moisture pockets, bedrock\) reflect a fraction of the wave energy back) Tj
T*
(   to a receiving antenna.) Tj
T*
(   - The receiver records two-way travel time \(t\) and amplitude, producing a continuous radargram) Tj
T*
(   profile.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Governing Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Relative Permittivity \(epsilon_r\): Controls wave propagation velocity:) Tj
T*
(   v = c / sqrt\(epsilon_r\). Depth of target: d = v * t / 2 = \(c * t\) / \(2 * sqrt\(epsilon_r\)\).) Tj
T*
(   Typical values: Air = 1, Dry concrete = 4-6, Wet concrete = 8-12, Water = 81.) Tj
T*
(   - Conductivity \(sigma\): Controls signal attenuation:) Tj
T*
(   alpha ~= 0.5 * sigma * sqrt\(mu / epsilon\) = 60*pi * sigma / sqrt\(epsilon_r\) \(Np/m\).) Tj
T*
(   High-conductivity media \(wet saline soil, moist concrete\) cause intense signal attenuation,) Tj
T*
(   severely restricting penetration depth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Trade-off between Resolution and Penetration Depth:) Tj
T*
(   - Resolution: delta_r ~= lambda / 4 = v / \(4 * f\).) Tj
T*
(   - High Frequency \(1.5 - 2.5 GHz\): Short wavelength provides millimeter resolution, ideal for) Tj
T*
(   locating shallow rebar and bridge deck delaminations \(depth < 0.5 m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Low Frequency \(100 - 400 MHz\): Lower attenuation gives deep penetration \(up to 5-10 m\) for) Tj
T*
(   geological surveying and dam bedrock assessment, but at coarse resolution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
