(   [Problem Statement]: A circular parallel-plate capacitor of radius R = 15 cm and plate separation d = 3.0 mm is charged by an AC source V\(t\) = 240*sqrt\(2\)*sin\(100*pi*t\) V. Determine: \(a\) capacitance C, \(b\) conduction current i_c\(t\), \(c\) displacement current density J_d\(t\), \(d\) induced magnetic field B at radius r = 10 cm.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Radius R = 0.15 m; Plate area A = pi * R^2 = pi * \(0.15\)^2 = 0.070686 m^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Separation d = 3.0 x 10^-3 m; epsilon_0 = 8.854 x 10^-12 F/m.) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage V\(t\) = V_0 * sin\(omega*t\), where V_0 = 240*sqrt\(2\) = 339.41 V, omega = 100*pi =) Tj
T*
(   314.16 rad/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Capacitance C:) Tj
T*
(   - C = epsilon_0 * A / d = \(8.854 x 10^-12 * 0.070686\) / \(3.0 x 10^-3\) = 2.086 x 10^-10 F =) Tj
T*
(   208.6 pF.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Conduction Current i_c\(t\):) Tj
T*
(   - i_c\(t\) = C * \(dV/dt\) = C * V_0 * omega * cos\(omega*t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Peak current: I_c0 = 2.086 x 10^-10 * 339.41 * 314.16 = 2.224 x 10^-5 A = 22.24 microamperes.) Tj
T*
(   - Expression: i_c\(t\) = 22.24 * cos\(100*pi*t\) microamperes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Displacement Current Density J_d\(t\):) Tj
T*
ET

