(   [Problem Statement]: A plane electromagnetic wave in air has electric field E\(z,t\) = 120*cos\(6*pi*10^8 t - beta*z\) i V/m. Calculate: \(a\) frequency f and wavelength lambda, \(b\) phase constant beta, \(c\) magnetic field expression H\(z,t\), \(d\) time-average Poynting vector S_avg.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - E\(z,t\) = 120 * cos\(omega*t - beta*z\) i V/m) Tj
T*
(   - Angular frequency omega = 6*pi x 10^8 rad/s) Tj
T*
(   - Free space parameters: c = 3.0 x 10^8 m/s, eta_0 = 377 Ohms) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Frequency f and Wavelength lambda:) Tj
T*
(   - f = omega / \(2*pi\) = \(6*pi x 10^8\) / \(2*pi\) = 3.0 x 10^8 Hz = 300 MHz.) Tj
T*
(   - lambda = c / f = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / \(3.0 x 10^8\) = 1.0 meter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Phase Constant beta:) Tj
T*
(   - beta = omega / c = \(6*pi x 10^8\) / \(3.0 x 10^8\) = 2*pi rad/m ~= 6.283 rad/m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
