(   [Problem Statement]: Calculate the skin depth and wave velocity in copper \(sigma = 5.8 x 10^7 S/m, mu_r = 1\) at: \(a\) power frequency 60 Hz, \(b\) radio frequency 1 MHz, \(c\) microwave frequency 10 GHz.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Governing Formulas for Good Conductor:) Tj
T*
(   - Skin depth: delta = 1 / sqrt\( pi * f * mu * sigma \)) Tj
T*
(   - Phase velocity: v = omega / beta = \(2*pi*f\) * delta = sqrt\( 4*pi*f / \(mu * sigma\) \)) Tj
T*
(   - Constants: mu = mu_0 = 4*pi x 10^-7 H/m, sigma = 5.8 x 10^7 S/m.) Tj
T*
(   - Combined factor: pi * mu_0 * sigma = pi * \(4*pi x 10^-7\) * 5.8 x 10^7 = 2.2898 x 10^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Hence: delta = 1 / sqrt\(228.98 * f\) = 0.0661 / sqrt\(f\) meters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) At Power Frequency f = 60 Hz:) Tj
T*
(   - delta = 0.0661 / sqrt\(60\) = 0.0661 / 7.746 = 8.53 x 10^-3 m = 8.53 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - v = 2 * pi * 60 * 8.53 x 10^-3 = 3.22 m/s.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
