(   [Problem Statement]: A Ground Penetrating Radar antenna on a concrete bridge deck detects a reflection from a reinforcing steel bar with a two-way travel time of 3.2 ns. If dry concrete has epsilon_r = 6.25 and mu_r = 1: \(a\) find wave velocity in concrete, \(b\) calculate the depth of the rebar, \(c\) determine the wavelength of the 1.5 GHz GPR signal in the concrete.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Two-way travel time: t = 3.2 ns = 3.2 x 10^-9 s.) Tj
T*
(   - Concrete properties: epsilon_r = 6.25, mu_r = 1.0.) Tj
T*
(   - Radar frequency: f = 1.5 GHz = 1.5 x 10^9 Hz.) Tj
T*
(   - Speed of light: c = 3.0 x 10^8 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Wave Velocity in Concrete v:) Tj
T*
(   - v = c / sqrt\(epsilon_r * mu_r\) = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / sqrt\(6.25\) = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / 2.5 = 1.20 x 10^8) Tj
T*
(   m/s = 0.12 m/ns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Depth of the Rebar d:) Tj
T*
(   - Since t is the two-way travel time \(antenna to rebar and back\):) Tj
T*
(   d = v * t / 2 = \(1.20 x 10^8 m/s * 3.2 x 10^-9 s\) / 2 = 0.384 / 2 = 0.192 m = 19.2 cm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Wavelength in Concrete lambda_c:) Tj
T*
(   - lambda_c = v / f = \(1.20 x 10^8 m/s\) / \(1.5 x 10^9 Hz\) = 0.080 m = 8.0 cm.) Tj
T*
(   - \(In free space, lambda_0 = c / f = 3.0x10^8 / 1.5x10^9 = 0.20 m = 20 cm\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Civil Structural Discussion:) Tj
T*
(   - The 19.2 cm depth corresponds precisely to the bottom rebar mat in a typical 25 cm thick deck) Tj
T*
(   slab. The 8.0 cm wavelength provides adequate resolution \(lambda/4 = 2 cm\) to distinguish) Tj
T*
(   individual 25 mm diameter rebars spaced at 15 cm intervals.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
