(   [Problem Statement]: A plane wave in air with electric field amplitude 50 V/m impinges normally on a wet soil boundary \(epsilon_r = 16, mu_r = 1, sigma = 0\). Calculate: \(a\) reflection coefficient Gamma, \(b\) transmission coefficient tau, \(c\) reflected and transmitted electric field amplitudes, \(d\) percentage of power reflected and transmitted.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Intrinsic Impedances of Media:) Tj
T*
(   - Medium 1 \(air\): eta_1 = eta_0 = 377 Ohms.) Tj
T*
(   - Medium 2 \(soil\): eta_2 = eta_0 / sqrt\(epsilon_r2\) = 377 / sqrt\(16\) = 377 / 4 = 94.25 Ohms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Reflection Coefficient Gamma:) Tj
T*
(   - Gamma = \(eta_2 - eta_1\) / \(eta_2 + eta_1\) = \(94.25 - 377\) / \(94.25 + 377\) = -282.75 / 471.25) Tj
T*
(   = -0.60.) Tj
T*
(   - The negative sign indicates a 180-degree phase shift upon reflection.) Tj
T*
ET

