(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the magnetic vector potential A and electric scalar potential V wave equations in the Lorenz gauge from Maxwell's equations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Magnetic Vector Potential A:) Tj
T*
(   - From Gauss's law for magnetism: Del dot B = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since the divergence of any curl is zero, B can be defined as the curl of a vector potential) Tj
T*
(   A: B = Del x A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Electric Scalar Potential V:) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute B into Faraday's law: Del x E = - d/dt \(Del x A\) => Del x \(E + dA/dt\) = 0.) Tj
T*
ET

