() Tj
T*
(   3. Substituting into Maxwell's First Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Del dot E = rho / epsilon => Del dot \( - Del V - dA/dt \) = rho / epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   - - Del^2\(V\) - d/dt \(Del dot A\) = rho / epsilon => Del^2\(V\) + d/dt \(Del dot A\) = - rho /) Tj
T*
(   epsilon.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Substituting into Maxwell's Fourth Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Del x B = mu*J + mu*epsilon * \(dE/dt\).) Tj
T*
(   - Del x \(Del x A\) = mu*J + mu*epsilon * d/dt \( - Del V - dA/dt \).) Tj
T*
(   - Del\(Del dot A\) - Del^2\(A\) = mu*J - mu*epsilon*Del\(dV/dt\) - mu*epsilon*\(d^2A/dt^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Rearranging: Del^2\(A\) - mu*epsilon*\(d^2A/dt^2\) - Del [ Del dot A + mu*epsilon*\(dV/dt\) ] = -) Tj
T*
(   mu*J.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. The Lorenz Gauge Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - Set: Del dot A + mu*epsilon*\(dV/dt\) = 0 \(Lorenz Gauge\).) Tj
T*
(   - The equations decouple completely into symmetric inhomogeneous wave equations:) Tj
T*
(   Del^2\(A\) - mu*epsilon*\(d^2A/dt^2\) = - mu*J) Tj
T*
(   Del^2\(V\) - mu*epsilon*\(d^2V/dt^2\) = - rho / epsilon.) Tj
