(>> Solution to Question 26:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain radiation pressure and electromagnetic momentum. Derive the expression for radiation pressure on a flat perfectly reflecting surface at normal incidence.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Electromagnetic Momentum:) Tj
T*
(   - Maxwell showed that electromagnetic waves transport both energy and linear momentum.) Tj
T*
(   - For an energy packet U traveling at speed c in vacuum, the associated momentum is: p = U / c.) Tj
T*
(   - The volume momentum density of an EM field is: g = S / c^2 = epsilon_0 * \(E x B\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Radiation Pressure on Perfect Absorber:) Tj
T*
(   - When an EM wave carries energy Delta_U to a surface in time Delta_t, momentum transferred is) Tj
T*
(   Delta_p = Delta_U / c.) Tj
T*
(   - Force exerted: F = Delta_p / Delta_t = \(1 / c\) * \(Delta_U / Delta_t\) = P_incident / c.) Tj
T*
(   - Radiation pressure P_rad = F / Area = \(P_incident / Area\) / c = S_avg / c.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation for Perfectly Reflecting Surface:) Tj
T*
(   - On a perfect reflector, the wave is reflected backward with unchanged amplitude:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_p_incident = + U / c; Delta_p_reflected = - U / c.) Tj
T*
(   - By conservation of momentum, the momentum transferred to the wall is:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_p_wall = p_initial - p_final = \(U / c\) - \(- U / c\) = 2 * U / c.) Tj
T*
(   - Radiation force on the surface: F = \(2 / c\) * \(Delta_U / Delta_t\) = 2 * P_incident / c.) Tj
T*
(   - Radiation pressure at normal incidence:) Tj
T*
(   P_rad,reflect = 2 * S_avg / c.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Numerical Example:) Tj
T*
(   - For full sunlight \(S_avg = 1000 W/m^2\) on a mirror: P_rad = 2 * 1000 / \(3.0 x 10^8\) = 6.67 x) Tj
T*
(   10^-6 N/m^2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
