(   - Frequency f = 2.0 GHz = 2.0 x 10^9 Hz; omega = 2*pi*f = 1.2566 x 10^10 rad/s.) Tj
T*
(   - sigma = 2.0 x 10^-4 S/m; epsilon_r = 1.05; mu_r = 1.0.) Tj
T*
(   - epsilon = 1.05 * 8.854 x 10^-12 = 9.297 x 10^-12 F/m.) Tj
T*
(   - Loss tangent: tan\(delta\) = sigma / \(omega*epsilon\) = 2.0 x 10^-4 / \(1.2566 x 10^10 * 9.297 x) Tj
T*
(   10^-12\) = 2.0 x 10^-4 / 0.1168 = 1.712 x 10^-3 << 0.1 \(low-loss dielectric\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Attenuation Constant alpha:) Tj
T*
(   - For low-loss dielectric: alpha ~= 0.5 * sigma * sqrt\(mu / epsilon\) = 0.5 * sigma * \(eta_0 /) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\(epsilon_r\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - alpha = 0.5 * \(2.0 x 10^-4\) * \(377 / sqrt\(1.05\)\) = 1.0 x 10^-4 * \(377 / 1.0247\) = 3.679 x) Tj
T*
(   10^-2 Np/m.) Tj
T*
(   - In dB/km: Attenuation \(dB/km\) = 8.686 * alpha * 1000 = 8.686 * 0.03679 * 1000 = 319.6 dB/km.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Phase Velocity v:) Tj
T*
(   - v ~= c / sqrt\(epsilon_r\) = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / sqrt\(1.05\) = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / 1.0247 = 2.928 x 10^8) Tj
T*
(   m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Power Loss over d = 15 km:) Tj
T*
(   - Total attenuation in dB: A_total = 319.6 dB/km * 15 km = 4,794 dB.) Tj
T*
(   - Total power transmitted is practically 0% \(complete signal extinction due to severe heavy) Tj
T*
(   rain absorption at 2 GHz\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
