12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 28:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the physical principles and mathematical formulation of electromagnetic shielding effectiveness \(SE\) in civil data centers and shielded control rooms.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Shielding Effectiveness:) Tj
T*
(   - Shielding effectiveness \(SE\) measures the capability of a metallic barrier to attenuate) Tj
T*
(   incident electromagnetic fields:) Tj
T*
(   SE \(dB\) = 20 * log10\( E_incident / E_transmitted \) = 10 * log10\( P_incident / P_transmitted \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Three Mechanisms of Shielding:) Tj
T*
(   - \(1\) Absorption Loss \(A\): Attenuation of wave amplitude as it traverses shield thickness t due) Tj
T*
(   to ohmic dissipation \(skin effect\):) Tj
T*
(   A \(dB\) = 20 * log10\( exp\(t / delta\) \) = 8.686 * \(t / delta\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(2\) Reflection Loss \(R\): Attenuation resulting from impedance mismatch between ambient air) Tj
T*
(   \(eta_0 = 377 Ohms\) and the metallic shield \(eta_m << 1 Ohm\):) Tj
T*
(   R \(dB\) = 20 * log10\( |eta_0 / \(4 * eta_m\)| \).) Tj
T*
(   - \(3\) Multiple Internal Reflection Correction \(M\): Correction factor for thin shields where) Tj
T*
(   internal re-reflections occur before full absorption:) Tj
T*
(   M \(dB\) = 20 * log10| 1 - exp\(-2*t/delta\) | \(Negligible when t > delta\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Total Shielding Effectiveness:) Tj
T*
(   - SE_total = A + R + M \(dB\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Civil Design Case Study:) Tj
T*
(   - A 1.0 mm thick copper shield \(sigma = 5.8 x 10^7 S/m\) at f = 10 MHz:) Tj
T*
(   delta = 66.1 / sqrt\(10^7\) = 20.9 micrometers.) Tj
T*
(   Absorption loss: A = 8.686 * \(1.0 x 10^-3 / 20.9 x 10^-6\) = 8.686 * 47.8 = 415 dB.) Tj
T*
(   - This provides virtually absolute electromagnetic isolation against lightning surges and RF) Tj
T*
(   interference.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
