12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A lightning discharge delivers a current surge I\(t\) = 50*exp\(-t / 10^-5\) kA into a steel reinforced concrete foundation. Discuss the generation of transient magnetic and electric fields, skin effect in rebar, and induced step voltages.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Current Profile and Spectral Components:) Tj
T*
(   - Peak stroke current I_0 = 50 kA; decay time constant tau = 10 microseconds.) Tj
T*
(   - High di/dt at t = 0: di/dt|_0 = - I_0 / tau = - 50,000 / 10^-5 = - 5.0 x 10^9 A/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Frequency content spans from DC up to several megahertz \(f_eq ~ 1 / \(pi*tau\) ~ 30 kHz - 1) Tj
T*
(   MHz\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Induced Magnetic Field:) Tj
T*
(   - Around the foundation conductor at radial distance r:) Tj
T*
(   B\(r,t\) = mu_0 * I\(t\) / \(2*pi*r\).) Tj
T*
(   - At r = 1.0 m: B_peak = \(4*pi x 10^-7 * 50,000\) / \(2*pi * 1.0\) = 0.010 Tesla = 100 Gauss.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Skin Effect in Foundation Steel Rebar:) Tj
T*
(   - For structural steel \(mu_r ~ 300, sigma ~ 6.0 x 10^6 S/m\) at dominant surge frequency f ~ 100) Tj
T*
(   kHz:) Tj
T*
(   delta = 1 / sqrt\( pi * 10^5 * \(300 * 4*pi x 10^-7\) * 6.0 x 10^6 \) = 0.037 mm = 37 micrometers.) Tj
T*
(   - The current is forced into a microscopically thin outer skin of the 25 mm rebar, multiplying) Tj
T*
(   the effective surge impedance and creating hazardous transient potentials.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Induced Step Voltage on Ground Surface:) Tj
T*
(   - Current spreading into soil of resistivity rho_soil = 100 Ohm*m:) Tj
T*
(   E_r = rho_soil * J = rho_soil * I / \(2*pi*r^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step voltage between feet spaced Delta_r = 1.0 m apart \(from r1 = 2 m to r2 = 3 m\):) Tj
T*
(   V_step = Integral_2^3 E_r dr = \(rho_soil * I / 2*pi\) * [ 1/2 - 1/3 ] = \(100 * 50,000 / 2*pi\) *) Tj
T*
(   \(1/6\) = 132.6 kV.) Tj
T*
(   - This lethal potential difference necessitates equipotential grounding meshes in all civil) Tj
T*
(   infrastructure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
